  "title": "Docker sandbox provider for `osf sandbox run`",
  "summary": "Adds a provider-neutral sandbox seam (`Sandbox` trait, spec/command validation, an in-memory fake) and a Docker adapter that implements it by shelling out to `docker` one invocation per operation. A new `osf sandbox run` subcommand plans a run from `--repo`/`--state`/`--image`, validates it before any docker call, then creates a container, runs one command inside it, and always removes it — including on SIGINT/SIGTERM, which a signal watcher turns into a removal plus exit 130/143.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
